---
title: Chocolate Pot de Crème
description: Dark chocolate custard cooked sous vide in jars, topped with an Oreo crumble.
tags: [custard, sous-vide]
course: dessert
cuisine: French
source:
  name: ChefSteps
  url: https://www.chefsteps.com/recipes/chocolate-pot-de-creme-y-all
adapted: true
servings: 5
time: 10h
---

Fill the #sous vide container{} with water, full enough for the #circulator{} to operate properly.

Add the circulator into the water and set it to 158°F (70°C).

Separate the @egg yolks{110%g}(4 oz, about 7) from the whites, weighing the yolks on a #digital scale{} (keep the whites for other recipes like homemade marshmallows).

Heat the @ultra-pasteurized heavy cream{550%g}(20 oz) in a #medium saucepan{} over medium heat until it reaches 158°F (70°C) on a #digital thermometer{}.

Add the @dark chocolate{175%g}(6 oz, 70%) pieces and allow them to melt while stirring slowly.

Blend the melted chocolate and heated heavy cream with an #immersion blender{} on low until smooth.

Remove the pot from the heat.

Add the @granulated sugar{115%g}(4 oz), @iodized table salt{4%g}(0.15 oz), and @&egg yolks{} to the pot while stirring slowly.

Blend everything in the pot with the immersion blender on low until smooth.

Place a #fine-mesh strainer{} over a #bowl{} and strain the mixture into it.

Rest for ~rest{30%minutes} to allow air bubbles to rise to the surface.

Skim off any air bubbles that remain on the surface after the rest.

Fill each of the #canning jars{5}(8 oz, with lids) to about 1/2 inch (1.25 cm) from the top.

If any air bubbles appear, tap the filled jar on a surface gently until they burst.

Seal each jar with its lid, tightening only to "fingertip tight" (see the note below).

> **Fingertip tight** — This is a rough one to describe. In general, many folks adhere to the following…

> 1. Put the band on top of the canning jar and lid.

> 2. Turn it until you feel resistance.

> 3. Turn one-quarter more then stop.

> 4. Once the ring stops turning freely — and you don't want to put too much pressure on it — then it's tight enough.

Lower the jars into the at-temperature water with a #jar lifter{}(or tongs) and make sure they are fully submerged.

Allow the jars to cook via sous vide for ~cook{1%hour}.

Remove the jars from the water. Dry them and place them in the fridge to chill until cold (overnight or the day before is best).

Serve from the fridge, topped with @?./oreo-cookie-crumble{}, whipped cream, or other toppings.
